<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Hassum</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 BCE – 1630 BCE (approx.) · capital Hassum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Hassum, a wealthy kingdom west of the upper Euphrates, ally of Aleppo, whose gods were carried off to Hattusa by the Hittite king Hattusili I.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Hashshum lay in the borderlands of northern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> and south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. It is mentioned in the Old Assyrian trade letters and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/mari">Mari</a> archives as a kingdom on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravan-trade">caravan routes</a>, closely tied to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yamhad">Yamhad</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Little is known of its internal government. The texts show it as a prosperous city with temples of the storm god and his consort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebat">Hebat</a>, reflecting the Hurrian and Syrian culture of the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In the 17th century BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hattusili-i">Hattusili I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> defeated the armies of Hassum and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, sacked the city and carried its divine statues, wagons and treasures to the temple of the sun goddess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arinna">Arinna</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1800 BCE – 1630 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:23.88%;width:3.38%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 BCE – 1630 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/17th-century-bce">17th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hassum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hurrian and Syrian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Hurrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hassuwa, Hashshum</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-1715&amp;focus=hassum" aria-label="Hassum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5526 755 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hassum lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5935 1127h0M5852 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5846 1011h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5846 1011h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Turkey. <a href="/atlas?year=-1715&amp;focus=hassum">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

